    {
      "claim": "The query's physicochemical profile (MW 592 Da, TPSA 155.5 Å², 4 HBD/7 HBA, 14 rotatable bonds, zero neutral fraction at pH 7.4, logD 0.77) is consistent with the low-permeability/efflux phenotype measured for structurally related large polar ionizable molecules.",
      "card_ids": ["C169","C165","C202","C203"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 Caco-2 data for large polar ionizable molecules show low absorptive permeability and strong efflux: aliskiren A-to-B 0.48 ± 0.15 ×10^-7 cm/s with B-to-A 20.21 ± 1.10 ×10^-7 cm/s (flux ratio 42.4); a peptide-like carboxylate/amide prodrug has AP-to-BL 1.80 ± 0.89 ×10^-8 cm/s and BL-to-AP 10.4 ± 0.80 ×10^-8 cm/s.",
      "card_ids": ["C169","C162","C192","C165","C186","C154","C163"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall efflux records for related carboxylate/amide/urea compounds show very low absorptive Papp and high efflux ratios: M01 Papp 4 nm/s with ER 51; M12 AP-BL 0.0564 ×10^-6 cm/s with ER 67; M09 A-B 0.8 ×10^-6 cm/s with ER 16; repaglinide is a P-gp substrate.",
      "card_ids": ["C202","C219","C229","C203","C213","C238","C243","C204","C207","C206","C216","C224","C239","C240"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance records for repaglinide, a carboxylate/amide/aryl-ether molecule sharing key ionizable and metabolic motifs with the query, show measurable intrinsic clearance (hepatocyte CLint,u 5.5 µL/min/10^6 cells; rat/porcine microsomal CLint ~24.8–30.2 µL/min/mg), CYP2C8/3A4 oxidative metabolism, and acyl-glucuronide formation (scaled CLint 15.6 µL/min/g liver). This is mechanistically supportive of hepatic presystemic loss, though not by itself threshold-determining.",
      "card_ids": ["C245","C246","C257","C260","C294","C293","C281","C277","C252"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Integrated with the query's poor-permeability/efflux phenotype, the hepatic metabolism evidence affirmatively supports F < 20%; distant L1/L2 high-F contexts do not provide query-specific evidence to override this.",
      "card_ids": ["C169","C165","C202","C203","C245"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C245","C246","C257","C260","C294","C293","C281","C277","C252"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific Caco-2/PAMPA, solubility, efflux, or hepatic clearance data are available; L4/L5/L6 records are for reference molecules.",
    "Transferability of reference-molecule permeability/efflux and hepatic metabolism evidence to the query is inferred from shared physicochemical and structural features, not direct measurement.",
    "Hepatic clearance alone is not threshold-sufficient; the low-F conclusion depends on combining it with the low-permeability/efflux evidence.",
    "L1/L2 high-F contexts are structurally distant and not applicable to the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low and strengthened: L4/L5 showed coherent low permeability and strong efflux for structurally related large, polar, fully ionized molecules; L6 adds hepatic clearance/metabolic-stability evidence for a related carboxylate/amide/aryl-ether molecule (repaglinide), supporting hepatic presystemic loss. Together with the query's MW 592 Da, TPSA 155.5 Å², 4 HBD/7 HBA, 14 rotatable bonds, and full ionization at pH 7.4, this affirmatively supports F < 20%; distant L1/L2 high-F contexts do not override this evidence."
}

